###Mapping
// Code translations, extracted so more than one mapping can share them.
//
// SideMapping used to live inside trading::TradingMapping. reporting::EmbeddedFlatMapping
// needs it too, but cannot `include trading::TradingMapping` — that would bring the
// canonical trading::Trade -> TRADE mapping with it and leave two root mappings for the
// same class in one Mapping, which is ambiguous. Duplicating the code map instead would
// let the two copies drift, and the invariance test would then be comparing two different
// translations rather than two mappings of one translation.
Mapping trading::Codes
(
    // Source codes, not labels — which is how every real trade store stores side.
    // 'BOT' is a legacy code kept alive by an old feed: two source values collapsing
    // onto one enum value is the case a naive code->label map gets wrong.
    trading::Side: EnumerationMapping SideMapping
    {
        BUY: ['B', 'BOT'],
        SELL: ['S']
    }
)
